        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T14:20:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In theory, %.9g is the perfect format string for round-tripping values safely. However, in practice, both %.9g and %.8g introduced nonsense rounding-error data and re-bloated the values. With %.7g we actually get input that looks like the original program.\n\nMaybe if `Literal::description()` used `%.9g` as well...? I could experiment with that.\n\n%.8g: http://screen/4muehFbAcXx38py\n\n%.9g: http://screen/4Vo2WpLauNeDSJZ",
      "parentUuid": "ebdb2c68_6e60e53d",
      "revId": "94c4162c70d24ff40c5b69a49cb79077fbfb3c45",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
